From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:18:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/34] surface lazy: one image for a surface's textures

A compositor's sampled-only texture over a surface's pages was a linear
image in place, with no standing of its own: its read met the bytes, so
the writer's whole surface went back every frame. A texture made over
pages a lazy surface's first shadow covers now binds that image and its
copies under its own record, where the extent, levels, layers, samples,
type, hazard tracking, usage, offset and rows fit and the image takes a
view of its format. It holds the first texture's texels, as the copies'
way back is weak. Anything else keeps today's path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
